{"id": "EUVD-2026-26651", "enisaUuid": "99546396-ca75-34c8-8579-33407cc15b8b", "description": "In the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\nwifi: mac80211: check tdls flag in ieee80211_tdls_oper\n\nWhen NL80211_TDLS_ENABLE_LINK is called, the code only checks if the\nstation exists but not whether it is actually a TDLS station. This\nallows the operation to proceed for non-TDLS stations, causing\nunintended side effects like modifying channel context and HT\nprotection before failing.\n\nAdd a check for sta->sta.tdls early in the ENABLE_LINK case, before\nany side effects occur, to ensure the operation is only allowed for\nactual TDLS peers.", "datePublished": "2026-05-01T14:15:46", "dateUpdated": "2026-10-15T01:18:53", "baseScore": 0.0, "references": ["https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/e602246235fc2ef06c39b2e9cf147d84d0896b73", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/6813a8b1b240756dad4375f3e020ce10e4e3871b", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/44839ea7e96b3659a1606f3d5267063135479b7c", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/ba5b43db126a5e7378553869e3f7954d9187349f", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/8148c2fda4ebb17104a573649c9b699208ad10ee", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/be81f17151fcb8546a95f35ca8f4231b065985de", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/e77b2937aaa20264e4bd699d3244bdb50e7e3343", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/7d73872d949c488a1d7c308031d6a9d89b5e0a8b"], "aliases": ["GHSA-j5xm-hgh6-vq4q", "CVE-2026-43052"], "assigner": "Linux", "epss": 0.18, "enisaIdProduct": [{"id": "090bdf51-2bb4-3e26-92cb-3b76d5c09568", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "941c93cd039852b7ab02c74f4698c99d82bd6cfe <44839ea7e96b3659a1606f3d5267063135479b7c"}, {"id": "10047a3d-a1ab-350b-803b-b16231dd0dd3", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 5.10.259"}, {"id": "1dc75839-cd44-3ca3-a31e-7d449bb5b87a", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 7.0"